From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac-build <b@steamac>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:26:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: sparse residency through views with baseMipLevel > 0, and
 of gathers

Metal reports the residency of a sparse operation through a texture view
with baseMipLevel > 0 for the image's level or LOD without the base (the
data is right): fetches and explicit LODs measure the image's level, a
storage view's reads level 0, gradient and implicit LODs (computed from
the image's size) only miss the base in their clamps. Sparse gathers are
reported resident when footprint texels across a tile edge are not (their
values are zero), and measured at the sampler's minLod level.

Views with baseMipLevel > 0 of sparse residency images get residency views
of the same levels and all levels below them (sampled and storage
descriptors carry them; storage image descriptors grow to 16 bytes).
Sparse operations through such views take their residency from the same
operation on the residency view at level/LOD + base: fetches and imageLoad
at level + base, explicit LODs with the sampler's clamps applied in the
shader (Metal's order) and sampled through a copy of the sampler without
LOD clamps, made only when they could matter; gradient and implicit LODs
(as gradients of the coordinates, taken where the sample is) as gradients
scaled to the view's LOD + base with the clamps as min_lod_clamp, or an
explicit LOD at maxLod when the view's isotropic LOD is past it; min/max
reduction samples with their LOD limited to the view, + base. Gathers, on
any view, take their residency from a bilinear sample of their level
through a LINEAR copy of the sampler without clamps. Other views pay a
descriptor load and a branch per sparse operation.
---
